+# Implementation Plan: Rental Module
+
+**Spec**: [spec.md](spec.md) | **Date**: 2026-10-22
+
+## Summary
+
+A dependency-free TypeScript module exposing `createRentalService()` from `src/index.ts`; in-memory maps for equipment and bookings.
+
+## Technical Context
+
+- Language: TypeScript (strict, NodeNext ESM), no runtime dependency
+- Testing: `node --test` (package.json `test` script); tests in `test/` as `.test.ts`, run via Node's native TypeScript type stripping where available
+- Storage: in memory
+- Constitution: `.specify/memory/constitution.md` is still the unfilled template, so it imposes no rules. Gate passes (re-checked after design).
+
+## Design
+
+- `src/index.ts`: service and types in one file (avoids relative-import extension issues between tsc NodeNext and Node type stripping).
+- Period parsing: strict regex for ISO-8601 UTC (`...Z`), `Date.parse`, require ms divisible by 86 400 000 (UTC midnight), end > start; days = diff / 86 400 000. Output normalised with `toISOString()`.
+- Total = days × dailyPrice (safe integers checked).
+- Overlap: existing.start < new.end && new.start < existing.end, per item; half-open intervals so back-to-back is fine.
+- Booking record keeps start/end/total (FR-008) for the future cancellation feature; ids are sequential strings.
+- Validation happens fully before any state mutation.
+
+See [research.md](research.md), [data-model.md](data-model.md), [quickstart.md](quickstart.md).
