+# Feature Specification: Rental Module
+
+**Feature Branch**: `001-rental-module`
+**Created**: 2026-10-22
+**Status**: Draft
+**Input**: Rental module for the booking desk: in-memory service to register equipment, quote and book rentals.
+
+## User Scenarios & Testing *(mandatory)*
+
+### User Story 1 - Quote a rental (Priority: P1)
+
+Desk staff register boards and sails with a daily price, then ask what renting an item for a period costs.
+
+**Independent Test**: Add an item at 2500 cents/day, quote 3 days, expect total 7500.
+
+**Acceptance Scenarios**:
+
+1. **Given** a registered item, **When** quoting a whole-day period of N days, **Then** total = N × daily price, in integer cents.
+2. **Given** an unknown item, **When** quoting, **Then** the request is rejected with an error.
+3. **Given** a period not starting/ending at midnight UTC, empty, reversed, or not valid ISO-8601 UTC, **When** quoting, **Then** it is rejected.
+
+### User Story 2 - Book a rental (Priority: P1)
+
+Desk staff book an item for a period and get a booking with an identifier and the total.
+
+**Independent Test**: Book an item, then try to book it again for an overlapping period: second attempt is rejected.
+
+**Acceptance Scenarios**:
+
+1. **Given** a free item, **When** booking, **Then** a booking `{id, itemId, start, end, total}` is returned with a unique id and the quoted total.
+2. **Given** an existing booking, **When** booking the same item for an overlapping period, **Then** it is rejected.
+3. **Given** an existing booking, **When** booking the same item for a period starting exactly when it ends (or ending exactly when it starts), **Then** it succeeds.
+4. **Given** an existing booking, **When** booking a different item for the same period, **Then** it succeeds.
+
+### Edge Cases
+
+- Invalid equipment on `addEquipment` (non-string/empty id, kind other than board/sail, non-integer or negative price, duplicate id) is rejected.
+- A rejected booking leaves no trace; failed attempts never block later bookings.
+- Bookings in the past are not specially restricted (assumption below).
+
+## Requirements *(mandatory)*
+
+### Functional Requirements
+
+- **FR-001**: System MUST let staff register equipment `{id, kind: 'board'|'sail', dailyPrice}`.
+- **FR-002**: System MUST quote `{itemId, start, end}` returning `{itemId, start, end, total}`.
+- **FR-003**: System MUST book the same request, returning `{id, itemId, start, end, total}`.
+- **FR-004**: Money MUST be integer euro cents.
+- **FR-005**: Times MUST be ISO-8601 UTC strings; periods MUST start and end at midnight UTC, with end the start of the day after the last day, and cover at least one day.
+- **FR-006**: Quote and book MUST reject unknown items and disallowed periods; book MUST also reject when the item is not free for the whole period.
+- **FR-007**: The same item MUST never hold two bookings with overlapping periods.
+- **FR-008**: Each booking MUST keep its start and total so the cancellation policy (under 24 h before start: no refund; otherwise full refund) can be applied later. Cancellation itself is out of scope now.
+
+### Key Entities
+
+- **Equipment**: id, kind (board/sail), daily price in cents.
+- **Booking**: id, item, period, total in cents.
+
+## Success Criteria *(mandatory)*
+
+- **SC-001**: Every quote equals days × daily price exactly, with no fractional cents.
+- **SC-002**: No two bookings of one item ever overlap, however requests are ordered.
+- **SC-003**: Every invalid request (unknown item, off-midnight, empty period, conflict) is refused.
+
+## Assumptions
+
+- State lives in memory only; it is lost on restart.
+- Period start and end are given in the canonical form `YYYY-MM-DDT00:00:00.000Z`, or any ISO-8601 UTC string denoting midnight; returned values are normalised to that canonical form.
+- Equipment ids are unique; there are no taxes, discounts or deposits.
+- Past dates are allowed (no clock is consulted until cancellation is built).
